  "description": "One class per minimal API endpoint, discovered and mapped for you: implement IEndpoint<TGroup, TResponse> (method, route, handler) and IEndpointGroup (prefix, tags), call app.MapEndpoints(assemblies), and every endpoint is mapped into its group with its name, its 200 response type, its error responses (401/403 whenever the endpoint ends up requiring authorization, 429 whenever it is rate limited, 413 for uploads), and per-endpoint opt-ins for authorization, rate limiting, file uploads and file downloads. Endpoints are listed at compile time by a source generator, so there is no assembly scan at startup and a broken endpoint is a build error. Your own error schema (ProblemDetails by default), group and endpoint conventions for app-wide rules, and an extension point for request validation (see Hlibz.MinimalApi.Endpoints.FluentValidation).",
